 'TOGO M3211 is Formate medium and its NaCOOH row denotes sodium formate. The false marine-medium caption is corrected. Provider-enriched adjacent ontology fields are not independent primary evidence; the exact literal and primary locator remain on the formate owner.',
 'DSMZ 87 salt preparation has a source-specific MICRO:0001830 term, but the complete source comparison retains the recorded historical sulfide/formula differences. The term does not approve copying all historical ontology composition into the recipe or lifting source holds.',
 'CCAP E27/E31/E31 ANT and TAP establish damaged typography for MgSO4·7H2O. Separately, NBRC 406 itself prints MgSO2·7H2O in the main recipe, so automated TOGO enrichment is not a correction authority. Three MgSO2 literals are rejected on the heptahydrate owner; six hydration-unspecified inherited aliases remain structured, conditional and unapproved pending their original occurrence-stage provenance.',
 'The source So(Sulfur Powder) is elemental sulfur powder, with explicit source context rather than a sulfate or sulfide reagent. Preserve the exact label and physical form; the source-specific URL replaces campaign-only alias provenance.',
 'The five NBRC contexts explicitly use a one-water thiamine-HCl spelling. The exact chloride/protonation stoichiometry, reagent identifier and structure remain unresolved. An existing anhydrous or dihydrate record cannot absorb these labels as an exact form solely from the shared thiamine name.',
 'RibofIavin is source typography for riboflavin. Separately DSMZ 1157 and NBRC 1604 dose aliquots of 0.2 mg/ml and 0.05 microgram/ml preparations. Those supplied-stock labels are rejected only as exact synonyms of the neat molecular owner, preserving their original source/type history.',
 'Three TOGO sources explicitly place MnCI2.4H2O in the manganese chloride tetrahydrate context. The apparent capital-I typo is resolved by the complete source table and formula, with all three primary locators retained. No less hydrated form or generic manganese ion is substituted.',
 'JCM 403 supplies 10 mg thiamine HCl in 100 ml of 25 mM phosphate buffer at pH 3.4. Shared composition supports the existing preparation anchor. Filtration is asserted only where NBRC 1321 or JCM 1125 explicitly says so; JCM 403 does not supply that instruction.',
 'TOGO M3129 names ground sulfur powder. This is the elemental solid input, not a sulfur-containing mixture or dissolved species; the exact source label receives its own primary locator while sharing the supported sulfur owner.',
 'The complete ATCC 1256 recipe defines the selected preparation; its numbered source is provenance, not the sole identity justification. Preserve the explicit input table and preparation stage without treating the whole medium as a pure constituent or adopting unrelated receiving-medium additions.',
 'JCM 1130 defines the VFA preparation used in YCFA. The listed acids, amounts and preparation are retained as batch facts. This mixture is not the generic fatty-acid ontology class or the independently specified JCM 266 stock.',
 'P5 names Niacin (B3) within a separately prepared vitamin stock. That literal identifies the neutral vitamin input, not the whole carrier preparation. Independently, CHEBI:32544 establishes Nicotinate as the charged conjugate base, so only that inherited exact-identity synonym is rejected on neutral nicotinic acid.',
 'Both NBRC sources name 1 M HEPES-KOH and dose 20 ml; 7.14 and 9.0 are receiving-medium pH values. Missing stock pH, solvent or neutralization ratio establishes neither equality nor difference. The two handles remain conditional. NEW-02 removes inferred moiety/species material components while retaining the bounded nominal stock description.',
 'JCM 1030 defines a ferrihydrite suspension by preparation and resuspension with 200 ml water. This is not an explicit 200 ml final-volume instruction or a measured solids concentration. Retain the suspension as a whole preparation and keep its 200 ml receiving dose separate from preparation water.',
 'NBRC 1321 footnote ***** explicitly defines the buffered thiamine stock and filter sterilization. The frozen NBRC_1323 filename is not the primary medium number. Preserve that source-specific processing and the shared composition, without transferring filtration into sources that omit it.',
 'DSMZ 524 and 623 name Na-meta silicate without supplier/hydration in the recipe texts. Provider CAS enrichment is not a historical reagent certificate. Existing anhydrous and nonahydrate candidates do not settle the source form; no exact alias or duplicate owner is justified from the omission alone.',
 'The sludge-fluid preparation is resolved through DSMZ 119 and its actual treatment, not by equating sludge with clarified rumen fluid. The frozen thermophilic substitution context is retained with its exact receiving dose and source route; whole-medium composition is not inferred from that dose.',
 'CCAP TAP establishes the lost-subscript MgSO 7H O input as magnesium sulfate heptahydrate. This supports only that source damaged label. It does not prove that the six unrelated inherited generic magnesium-sulfate aliases denote the same hydrate.',
 'TOGO M2577 explicitly names thiamine pyrophosphate at 0.2% w/v in water as a supplied preparation. Retain the whole-stock boundary and exact literal; it is not neat TPP and does not resolve the distinct chloride-free/chloride source identity disputes.',
