 'Both official ATCC 2811 sheets name one ml Wolfe mineral elixier without a formula or unambiguous cross-reference. Searches found candidate Wolfe preparations but no authoritative link to one of them. The missing fact is which whole preparation the source means; ingredient CURIE uncertainty alone would not justify this hold.',
 'JCM 221 modified Wolfe has the same thirteen non-water input amounts as ATCC 1190/1191. Its omitted hydration and KOH strength cannot prove a different mixture. Preserve the listed 1000 ml water versus ATCC final-volume instruction separately; coordinator family reconciliation remains pending.',
 'The source Guanine HCl row lacks a supplier and hydration certificate. Free attempts to retrieve the Merlen full paper failed; a snippet is not a complete recipe. Current TCI and Sigma comparators establish a 1:1 salt but allow water loss and do not identify the historical supplied form. No exact anhydrous/hydrate selection follows.',
 'The eleven TOGO DSMZ ethanol contexts trace K1 and K3 uses to DSMZ 78/104/110; the nested 212a case is the twelfth route. The common nominal 95% name is retained without a v/v or aqueous-balance assertion. Receiving dilution and variant medium recipes do not prove separate supplied ethanols.',
