 'NBRC 1507 independently prints Thiamine-HCl·H2O. Its unresolved chloride/protonation and supplier identity is assessed separately from the other NBRC monohydrate occurrences. The literal is retained rather than silently normalized to anhydrous thiamine hydrochloride or the dihydrate.',
 'JCM 411 defines poorly crystalline iron(III) oxide by precipitation, washing and resuspension. This supports a source-defined preparation even when exact mineral phase, retained ions and final solids concentration are unresolved. Its ferric input/procedure is not an exact molecular iron-oxide identity or the JCM 1030 recipe.',
